whelk (0.51.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Seal the Guile Scm value behind a private-field repr(transparent) newtype,
    so safe code cannot construct one from an arbitrary pointer.
  * Pin the pointer ABI with a layout test, and correct the unsafe figures in
    NEWS to 208 -> 113 crate-wide and 146 -> 55 in the Guile bridge.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.37.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Route every libguile call through the safe wrappers in guile/sys.rs; the
    unsafe token count falls from 208 to 113 and the Guile bridge from 146 to
    55, with the rest confined to the C ABI.
  * Export no #[no_mangle] symbols from the Rust crate, read the kernel release
    from procfs instead of uname, and wrap the GTK session-lock entry points in
    safe helpers.
  * Deny unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn and add tests for preference-key escaping, the
    PAM fallback policy, strict-mode spellings and the kernel release.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0100

whelk (0.36.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Rust bar folds trailing readings into a +N popover and opens the shell
    menu on a right-click over the bar's own gaps.
  * The Rust window title reads River's focused-view seat status, the launcher
    reads live application menu bars, and the Rust settings window, wallpaper
    picker, widget cards and night light are wired into the shell.
  * `cargo xtask install' now stages the Rust desktop entry and the shared
    hicolor icons as well as the binary and Scheme modules.
  * The release script checks and updates the Cargo manifests and runs the
    Rust formatting, clippy and workspace tests.
  * The C shell and its Meson install remain the default.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0100

  * The Rust shell preview now covers the bar and hardware readouts, launcher,
    clipboard, notifications, network panel, tray, global menu fallbacks,
    start menu, lock screen, wallpaper surfaces and the Scheme bridge.
  * Add the native wallpaper engine and picker, with per-monitor layer-shell
