whelk (0.34.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The shell owns the logind idle hint, its lock countdown, the
    presentation inhibitor and the do-not-disturb flag; the new inhibit
    module only reads `systemd-inhibit --list`.
  * `whelk --inhibit`, `--inhibit-reason` and `--idle-status` expose that
    manager, and the README explains the lock timer's decision.
  * The workspaces module reads niri's and Hyprland's IPC shapes, including
    the active workspace on each Hyprland monitor.
  * River's focused window is read from the river-status protocol; the
    window title is shown, and `{app-id}` stays empty because river does not
    publish one.
  * Module overrides are keyed by module kind and occurrence instead of bar
    position, so adding or reordering another kind cannot move a saved
    setting.  Positional keys from earlier releases are ignored.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.29.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The settings window gains a Modules page: every module on the first bar,
    with a Show switch and a typed editor for each of its options.
  * A Keys page edits the launcher's default mode and the prefix that selects
    each mode; an empty prefix disables one.
  * Module and launcher-key choices use the same reversible override file as
    the rest of the window, and Reset removes them all.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.28.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Hyprland is a session: the focused window comes from `hyprctl
    activewindow -j`, and close, full-screen, maximise, float and the move
    verbs go out through `hyprctl dispatch`.
  * River is a session for the window actions `riverctl` can carry out; its
    focused view is published only on the river-status protocol, so the
    window reading stays empty there.
  * Desktop widgets remember their dragged position per monitor, with the
    monitor-less position as the fallback for a screen that is gone.
  * A new inhibit module reads `systemd-inhibit --list` and names what is
    blocking sleep or idle, and why.
  * The settings window can open settings.scm at line 1 in $VISUAL/$EDITOR.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.27.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A menu being listed is told it is being listed: WHELK_RETV=0 is set on
    the generator's own environment instead of being inherited, so a menu
    opened from a chosen row no longer lists itself in the accepting mode.
  * The menu-script builder is shared by the listing and the choice, and the
    Scheme-free unit tests cover both calls.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.27.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The README documents the binary's linkage: what ldd and readelf show, why
    libpam is loaded at run time instead of linked, and the candidate order.
  * The lock screen section documents the three PAM failure modes behind
    "Authentication is unavailable", the log lines that tell them apart and the
    status codes treated as a wrong password.

